ScreenZen adds a wait before you open an app. For many people that wait works for a few weeks, then turns into something they tap through. A 2023 PNAS study of the similar app one sec measured this: the share of opens people dismissed fell from 43% in week 1 to about 32-34% by weeks 4-6. It also found the option to back out did more than the delay itself.

We compared the main ScreenZen alternatives using facts from their own App Store listings, checked November 2026: one sec and ClearSpace for a different style of delay, and Opal and Apple Screen Time for a harder stop. Prices are given as listed, with currency and billing period. Each app has its own if-then recommendation.

We make DeRot, a mid-scroll reset app, so we kept it out of the ranked list. It's built for a different moment: once the feed has already wound you up, rather than at the door. {url}
